{# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  app/views/_shared/_includes/case/material/action-plan-modal.njk

  Left-hand slide-out tray, shell recycled from notes-modal.njk (same
  overlay + role="dialog" panel + header/close-button structure, same
  data-action="close-*" trigger convention) — that shell has nothing
  notes-specific about it. The content is one action-plan-card.njk (or
  action-plan-list.njk — see the toggle below) per action, grouped under
  three headings: "Police initiated actions", "Triage and pre-charge
  actions" and "Post-charge actions".

  Not yet wired to a JS open/close controller (notes-modal.js's equivalent
  lives in material-viewer.js) — this is markup/structure only, matching
  what was asked for. The tray starts hidden and needs its own
  data-action="open-action-plan"-style trigger + show/hide script wired up
  separately when this is ready to go live.

  All three sections currently reuse the same card/row actions (Complete
  action/Withdraw, Change, Mark as complete, Mark as read) as skeleton
  placeholders — Triage/pre-charge's and Post-charge's real actions are
  still to be specified and will replace these once confirmed. Post-charge's
  three cards are titled "ROTI" as placeholders too, pending real names.

  Expected params:
    - actionPlanItems       : array of { type, status, requiredByDisplay,
                                          dateChaserSent, category,
                                          relatedSuspect, relatedMaterial,
                                          reasonForUpdate } — "Police
                                          initiated actions"
    - triagePreChargeItems  : same shape — "Triage and pre-charge actions"
    - postChargeItems       : same shape — "Post-charge actions"
------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}

